 **Security model**
 
-- Passwords hashed with scrypt; minimum 10 characters with letters and numbers; temporary passwords force a change at first login.
-- Server-side sessions in an `HttpOnly`, `SameSite=Lax` cookie (`Secure` automatically over HTTPS; force with `ERP_COOKIE_SECURE=1`). 2-hour idle / 12-hour absolute timeout (`ERP_SESSION_IDLE_MINUTES`, `ERP_SESSION_ABSOLUTE_HOURS`).
-- Every route is **deny-by-default** (`backend/auth/middleware.py`); role checks are repeated inside routers. Customer APIs never take a customer id from the request.
-- CSRF token required on every write, plus an Origin check. Login throttling: 5 failures per account / 20 per IP in 15 minutes.
-- Security headers (CSP, frame, nosniff, referrer, HSTS on HTTPS). Sign-ins, password changes and user changes are written to the audit log with the acting user and IP.
-- The server binds to `127.0.0.1` by default. To serve other machines set `ERP_HOST=0.0.0.0` **and** put it behind HTTPS (e.g. Caddy or nginx).
